§§ `s 32 Confirmation, s 33 Fraud and concealment, s 34 Mistake`

-- Time began 1 January 2020; last day 1 January 2026.
-- Signed written acknowledgment on 1 January 2022: the period ran 2 January 2020 to 31 December 2021 before it, 730
-- days, which do not count: 1 January 2028 (forks F1, F5).
#ASSERT `s 32 -- my last day after a confirmation` (`on` 1 1 2020) (`on` 1 1 2026) `acknowledged my right or title in writing, signed by them` (`on` 1 1 2022) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `on` 1 1 2028
#ASSERT `s 32 -- my last day after a confirmation` (`on` 1 1 2020) (`on` 1 1 2026) `made a payment to me in relation to my right or title` (`on` 1 1 2022) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `on` 1 1 2028
-- No 29 February in the uncounted days (time began 1 January 2021, last day 1 January 2027, acknowledgment 1 January
-- 2022): 364 days (2 January to 31 December 2021): 31 December 2027.
#ASSERT `s 32 -- my last day after a confirmation` (`on` 1 1 2021) (`on` 1 1 2027) `acknowledged my right or title in writing, signed by them` (`on` 1 1 2022) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `on` 31 12 2027
-- Acknowledgment the day after time began: no day ran before it.
#ASSERT `s 32 -- my last day after a confirmation` (`on` 1 1 2020) (`on` 1 1 2026) `acknowledged my right or title in writing, signed by them` (`on` 2 1 2020) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `on` 1 1 2026
#ASSERT `s 32 -- my last day after a confirmation` (`on` 1 1 2020) (`on` 1 1 2026) `acknowledged my right or title, but not in writing or not signed` (`on` 1 1 2022) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `on` 1 1 2026
#ASSERT `s 32 -- my last day after a confirmation` (`on` 1 1 2020) (`on` 1 1 2026) `neither` (`on` 1 1 2022) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `on` 1 1 2026
#ASSERT `s 32 -- my last day after a confirmation` (`on` 1 1 2020) (`on` 1 1 2026) `acknowledged my right or title in writing, signed by them` (`on` 1 1 2022) FALSE TRUE EQUALS `on` 1 1 2026
#ASSERT `s 32 -- my last day after a confirmation` (`on` 1 1 2020) (`on` 1 1 2026) `acknowledged my right or title in writing, signed by them` (`on` 1 1 2022) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `on` 1 1 2026
-- On the last day: 2191 days (2 January 2020 to 31 December 2025) do not count: 1 January 2032. The day after: too late.
#ASSERT `s 32 -- my last day after a confirmation` (`on` 1 1 2020) (`on` 1 1 2026) `acknowledged my right or title in writing, signed by them` (`on` 1 1 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `on` 1 1 2032
#ASSERT `s 32 -- my last day after a confirmation` (`on` 1 1 2020) (`on` 1 1 2026) `acknowledged my right or title in writing, signed by them` (`on` 2 1 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `on` 1 1 2026

-- Discovered 1 July 2021: the 546 days from 2 January 2020 to 30 June 2021 do not count: 1 July 2027.
#ASSERT `s 33 -- my last day after fraud or concealment` (`on` 1 1 2020) (`on` 1 1 2026) `my cause of action is based on fraud or deceit` TRUE FALSE (`on` 1 7 2021) EQUALS `on` 1 7 2027
#ASSERT `s 33 -- my last day after fraud or concealment` (`on` 1 1 2020) (`on` 1 1 2026) `a breach of duty was committed deliberately in circumstances where it was unlikely to be discovered for some time` TRUE FALSE (`on` 1 7 2021) EQUALS `on` 1 7 2027
#ASSERT `s 33 -- my last day after fraud or concealment` (`on` 1 1 2020) (`on` 1 1 2026) `a fact relevant to my cause of action, or who is liable, was deliberately concealed` TRUE FALSE (`on` 1 7 2021) EQUALS `on` 1 7 2027
#ASSERT `s 33 -- my last day after fraud or concealment` (`on` 1 1 2020) (`on` 1 1 2026) `none of these` TRUE FALSE (`on` 1 7 2021) EQUALS `on` 1 1 2026
#ASSERT `s 33 -- my last day after fraud or concealment` (`on` 1 1 2020) (`on` 1 1 2026) `my cause of action is based on fraud or deceit` FALSE FALSE (`on` 1 7 2021) EQUALS `on` 1 1 2026
#ASSERT `s 33 -- my last day after fraud or concealment` (`on` 1 1 2020) (`on` 1 1 2026) `my cause of action is based on fraud or deceit` TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 7 2021) EQUALS `on` 1 1 2026
#ASSERT `s 33 -- my last day after fraud or concealment` (`on` 1 1 2020) (`on` 1 1 2026) `my cause of action is based on fraud or deceit` TRUE FALSE (`on` 1 1 2019) EQUALS `on` 1 1 2026
-- Discovered after the period would have ended (s 33 (2)): 2556 days (2 January 2020 to 31 December 2026) do not
-- count, and the 6 years run from the discovery day itself: 31 December 2032.
#ASSERT `s 33 -- my last day after fraud or concealment` (`on` 1 1 2020) (`on` 1 1 2026) `my cause of action is based on fraud or deceit` TRUE FALSE (`on` 1 1 2027) EQUALS `on` 31 12 2032

#ASSERT `s 34 -- my last day after a mistake` (`on` 1 1 2020) (`on` 1 1 2026) TRUE FALSE (`on` 1 7 2021) EQUALS `on` 1 7 2027
#ASSERT `s 34 -- my last day after a mistake` (`on` 1 1 2020) (`on` 1 1 2026) TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 7 2021) EQUALS `on` 1 1 2026
#ASSERT `s 34 -- my last day after a mistake` (`on` 1 1 2020) (`on` 1 1 2026) FALSE FALSE (`on` 1 7 2021) EQUALS `on` 1 1 2026

§§ `Division 3.2 -- court extensions`

#ASSERT `s 36 -- can I ask the court to extend the time for my injury claim` `PI` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 36 does not apply to a claim to which s 16AA, s 16B or the Civil Law (Wrongs) Act 2002, part 3.1 applies (s 36 (5))`
#ASSERT `s 36 -- can I ask the court to extend the time for my injury claim` `PI` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the court may extend the time, for the period it decides, if it decides that is just and reasonable (s 36 (2)), even after the time has run out or the action has begun (s 36 (4))`
#ASSERT `s 36 -- can I ask the court to extend the time for my injury claim` `motor` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 36 does not apply to a claim to which s 16AA, s 16B or the Civil Law (Wrongs) Act 2002, part 3.1 applies (s 36 (5))`
#ASSERT `s 36 -- can I ask the court to extend the time for my injury claim` `motor` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 36 does not apply to a claim to which s 16AA, s 16B or the Civil Law (Wrongs) Act 2002, part 3.1 applies (s 36 (5))`
#ASSERT `s 36 -- can I ask the court to extend the time for my injury claim` `death` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 36 does not apply to a claim to which s 16AA, s 16B or the Civil Law (Wrongs) Act 2002, part 3.1 applies (s 36 (5))`
#ASSERT `s 36 -- can I ask the court to extend the time for my injury claim` `child health` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 36 does not apply to the 6-year period in s 30B (2) (s 36 (6))`
#ASSERT `s 36 -- can I ask the court to extend the time for my injury claim` `child health` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the court may extend the time, for the period it decides, if it decides that is just and reasonable (s 36 (2)), even after the time has run out or the action has begun (s 36 (4))`
#ASSERT `s 36 -- can I ask the court to extend the time for my injury claim` `abuse` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no need: the claim has no time limit (s 21C)`

#ASSERT `s 37 -- does the estate's distribution stop an extension` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the court must not extend the time under Division 3.2 (s 37)`
